Hi,

I have an Acer Extensa 3000 laptop and I can't get battery status or 
ac_adapter status, i.e. the /proc/acpi/battery and ac_adpater directories are 
empty. 

I've looked around on the web, and I found out about DSDT, so I tried to fix 
my table. I did sucessfully recompile it wthout errors and warnings, and 
included it in the kernel. But that did not help. Nor did applying the ECDT 
(my laptop does not provide a ECDT table, but is ACPI2.0 compliant) 
workaround. I even tracked down the acpi_os_name boot paramter and tried 
setting that to Microsoft Windows or Microsoft Windows XP, but it doesent 
help either. I have to admit I'm at the end of my wits here. 

I'm attaching the output of lspci -vv, my bios DSDT table, the one I fixed, my 
kernel log, the dmidump output and cat /proc/interrupts.

Any help would be greatly appreciated.

Johannes

